======================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- class (a): kernel and a_0 modifications
======================================================================================================================

  The 37 amplitude liabilities do not lie on any curve in the framework's own variable.  Over 20000
  relabellings the signed residual's correlation with log y has p = 0.982; the best NONPARAMETRIC function of
  y -- eight free numbers, more freedom than any kernel possesses -- takes the ledger from 0.461 to 0.397 dex
  while imposing an rms systematic of 0.216 dex on SPARC, whose own RAR point scatter is 0.176.

  The reason is local and can be read off the table: within 0.35 dex in y there are 12 pairs of systems whose
  required corrections differ by more than 0.6 dex, and SPARC points sit between them at zero.  The extreme
  case is ngc1052_df4 (-1.375 dex at y = 0.0582) against erass1_hiz (+0.408 at y = 0.0590).

  Every attempt below improves the ledger by less than half and breaks keepers as soon as it improves it at
  all.  The most flexible one does no better on the real ledger than on a shuffled one.

